For $S \subseteq D_\infty = \mathrm{InverseLimit}\,D\,P$, a natural candidate for an infimum in $D_\infty$ is built **coordinate by coordinate**: at index $n$, take the infimum in $D_n$ of the $n$-th coordinates of points in $S$.

**Definition (`inverseLimitSInfCoe`).** For **`S : Set (InverseLimit D P)`**,

$$(\texttt{inverseLimitSInfCoe}\,D\,P\,S)_n = \inf \{\, x_n \mid x \in S \,\}$$

in $D_n$ (Lean: **`sInf ((fun x => x.1 n) '' S)`**).

In the namespace **`inverseLimitSInfCoe`** we have

**Theorem (`apply`).** *For all **`S`**, **`n`**, the **`n`‑th coordinate of **`inverseLimitSInfCoe D P S`** is that stage infimum:*

$$\texttt{inverseLimitSInfCoe}\,D\,P\,S\,n = \inf \{\, x_n \mid x \in S \,\}.$$

*Proof.* Definition of **`inverseLimitSInfCoe`**. $\square$
